Till you want some more</i>


00:00:39.521 --> 00:00:43.252
<i>'Cause all I see is an open door</i>


00:00:43.425 --> 00:00:47.225
<i>And I see where it's leading me
All of this energy</i>


00:00:47.395 --> 00:00:50.990
<i>Been bottled up way too long
It's powerful, powerful</i>


00:00:51.166 --> 00:00:54.727
<i>You see what I'm getting at
I'm ready for all of that</i>


00:00:54.903 --> 00:00:58.430
<i>If I'm not a star, you're blind</i>


00:00:58.607 --> 00:01:01.974
<i>I've got rings on my fingers
And glitter in my hair</i>


00:01:02.144 --> 00:01:05.409
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:09.277
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:09.451 --> 00:01:13.478
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:13.655 --> 00:01:17.250
<i>I've got high heel stilettos
And I'm kicking in doors</i>


00:01:17.425 --> 00:01:20.553
<i>And kissing your ass
Ain't what my lipstick's for</i>


00:01:20.729 --> 00:01:24.495
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:24.666 --> 00:01:27.658
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:27.836 --> 00:01:31.328
Where's breakfast?
I want waffles, spaghetti!


00:01:31.506 --> 00:01:34.771
Spaghetti waffles! Whoo. Whoo!


00:01:34.943 --> 00:01:36.968
Victor. Victor.
Please wait in the house, please.


00:01:38.413 --> 00:01:41.246
My body is entering hunger shock.


00:01:42.617 --> 00:01:46.314
Oh, bad news.
The cat pooped in the den.


00:01:46.488 --> 00:01:49.787
Worse news, I used your blanket
to clean it up.


00:01:49.958 --> 00:01:51.892
- We don't have a cat.
- No kidding.


00:02:26.995 --> 00:02:30.556
Oh. L... Sorry.
I didn't think you'd be awake.


00:02:30.732 --> 00:02:31.892
You have an appointment...


00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:34.661
...with Guy Morgan,
I didn't think you'd wanna be late.


00:02:34.836 --> 00:02:37.771
Oh, look at you thinking. Cute.


00:02:37.939 --> 00:02:39.998
But I always have time for my portrait.


00:02:40.175 --> 00:02:41.699
Look alive. Paint.


00:02:42.143 --> 00:02:43.974
I'm feeling spiritually blocked.


00:02:44.145 --> 00:02:45.976
Draw me a sesame seed bath.


00:02:46.414 --> 00:02:47.540
Bath. Now.


00:02:48.516 --> 00:02:50.381
Now, make momma look more beautiful
and thinner.


00:02:51.753 --> 00:02:52.981
And make that water more quiet.


00:02:56.558 --> 00:02:58.651
- Bev, you awake?
- Of course I'm awake.


00:02:58.827 --> 00:03:01.421
If I waited for you, I'd never be on time.


00:03:01.596 --> 00:03:04.030
Lucky you never wait for me then.


00:03:17.512 --> 00:03:18.945
Victor, no.


00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.554
Uh, don't you want a glass?


00:03:27.722 --> 00:03:33.718
Hmm. Earthy. A tad fishy.
Lovely gravel finish.


00:03:34.195 --> 00:03:36.720
Did you let Victor put worms
in the blender again?


00:03:37.432 --> 00:03:39.127
Yes. I mean, no.


00:03:40.635 --> 00:03:42.227
I mean, it just happened.


00:03:42.771 --> 00:03:44.136
You know nothing can kill me.


00:03:45.307 --> 00:03:46.934
Nothing.


00:03:51.579 --> 00:03:54.446
Step on it, Katie.
I cannot be late for this meeting.


00:03:54.616 --> 00:03:55.981
Just run them over if you have to.


00:03:58.787 --> 00:04:01.813
Hello? No, the kids don't need a library.


00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:05.221
I am the dean, and the dean gets
what she wants, and I wanna remodel.


00:04:05.393 --> 00:04:08.851
You're just boring. I'm being honest.
I don't know what else to tell you.


00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:12.124
And I wanted my office done
for my meeting with Guy Morgan...


00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.961
...the music mogul, but no.


00:04:14.135 --> 00:04:16.330
And using Bollywood
as a theme for the dance?


00:04:16.504 --> 00:04:19.962
That's totally un-American.
I don't care if it was my idea.


00:04:21.643 --> 00:04:23.907
Hello.
Oh. Oh.


00:04:24.079 --> 00:04:26.775
I'm Dean Van Ravensway,
and you must be...


00:04:26.948 --> 00:04:30.042
- Guy Morgan.
- Ah, yes. Guy Morgan, a pleasure.


00:04:30.218 --> 00:04:31.708
You look like a man who knows things.


00:04:31.886 --> 00:04:34.446
Aha, even some things I shouldn't know.


00:04:34.622 --> 00:04:36.419
- And I'm Luke.
Great.


00:04:49.971 --> 00:04:53.930
<i>So tell me, Guy, is it true?
Are you the new judge on Idol?</i>


00:04:54.109 --> 00:04:57.476
Well, let's just say
that Randy may be in the doghouse.


00:04:57.645 --> 00:04:59.510
- Now, let's talk about my son.
- Of course.


00:04:59.681 --> 00:05:02.115
- Have you reviewed your schedule, Luke?
- Yes, I have.


00:05:02.283 --> 00:05:05.810
In fact, um, I'd like to add a music class.
Um, the music theory...


00:05:05.987 --> 00:05:09.548
Wellesley has a great business program.
That's why we're here.


00:05:10.058 --> 00:05:14.961
There are two types of people
in the music biz: Artists and businessmen.


00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:16.961
- Luke is a businessman.
- Of course.


00:05:17.465 --> 00:05:21.458
Katie, get in here. Look alive.
Make yourself useful.


00:05:24.939 --> 00:05:27.271
Luke is gonna need a tour of the campus.


00:05:27.742 --> 00:05:32.805
So text Bev and ask her
to escort Mr. Morgan around campus.


00:05:33.114 --> 00:05:36.242
Now, Luke, if you are half as talented
a producer as your father...


00:05:36.418 --> 00:05:39.478
The verdict's still out.
He hasn't earned it.


00:05:41.156 --> 00:05:43.420
Heard the story of how I started
in the music business?


00:05:43.591 --> 00:05:47.027
- Yes, everybody's heard it, Dad.
- Then everybody should know how it goes.


00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:51.524
There I was,
working for The Rolling Stones...


00:05:51.699 --> 00:05:53.530
...when Mick himself...
- Dad.


00:05:54.803 --> 00:05:58.000
Fine. As I said,
the verdict is still out on my son.


00:05:58.173 --> 00:06:01.939
He just produced an album
with the Fruity Dangers?


00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:03.771
Do you mean Danger Fruit?


00:06:04.946 --> 00:06:06.709
That record was amazing.


00:06:06.881 --> 00:06:09.850
I forgot what they were called because
they made me absolutely no money.


00:06:11.352 --> 00:06:13.820
Thank you. Rare I meet anyone
who's heard their album.


00:06:13.988 --> 00:06:16.889
What, are you kidding?
They're a cult phenomenon.


00:06:17.058 --> 00:06:18.719
I'm sorry. Why are you talking?


00:06:20.261 --> 00:06:25.824
What I need is for Luke to learn
to spot a commercially viable star.


00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.161
Image drives the bottom line, right?


00:06:28.336 --> 00:06:31.703
I feel you. Would we have Bieber Fever
if he were an ugly troll?


00:06:31.873 --> 00:06:34.034
Actually, he is a tad hobbit-like, isn't he?


00:06:34.209 --> 00:06:36.575
I'd like Luke
to produce your Semester Showcase...


00:06:36.744 --> 00:06:40.646
...to see if he can identify sellable talent.
- I produce the Semester Showcase.


00:06:41.783 --> 00:06:43.876
I will double your Showcase budget.


00:06:44.385 --> 00:06:46.751
I will invite every talent scout I know.


00:06:47.322 --> 00:06:49.449
This could be the beginning
of a relationship...


00:06:49.624 --> 00:06:51.592
...between Wellesley
and Kensington Records.


00:06:51.759 --> 00:06:53.750
Looks like we have a new producer.


00:06:53.928 --> 00:06:56.897
Oh, and this is my daughter, Bev.


00:06:57.332 --> 00:07:00.096
Bev, this is the platinum-selling,
Grammy-winning...


00:07:00.268 --> 00:07:03.169
...and very handsome producer,
Guy Morgan.


00:07:03.338 --> 00:07:05.169
Could you give his son, Luke, a tour?


00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:08.207
Sure. Would you like
to see the Wellesley perks?


00:07:08.376 --> 00:07:11.004
Um, yes, brilliant. Sure.


00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:13.470
- Katie.
I love your accent.


00:07:13.648 --> 00:07:15.240
Katie.
Wanna come over tonight?


00:07:15.416 --> 00:07:17.782
What are you still doing here? Go.


00:07:17.952 --> 00:07:21.353
Guy and I have things we need to discuss.
Out. Now.


00:07:21.956 --> 00:07:27.360
So, Guy, you've gotta tell me,
what was that like working under Mick?


00:07:36.237 --> 00:07:37.932
Watch out.


00:07:38.406 --> 00:07:40.431
- Dangerous balls.
- Ha, ha. Thanks.


00:07:41.442 --> 00:07:45.037
- So you womanned up and did it?
Hey!


00:07:45.213 --> 00:07:47.010
- Oh, I did it.
Hey!


00:07:47.181 --> 00:07:49.547
- What happened?
Can we have our ball?


00:07:49.717 --> 00:07:51.082
I didn't give my CD to Luke.


00:07:51.252 --> 00:07:54.244
I snuck it in his dad's bag.


00:07:54.422 --> 00:07:58.381
But Guy Morgan has your demo.
That's huge. What you need is a champion.


00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.289
No, what I need is to graduate.


00:08:01.129 --> 00:08:03.029
You giving our ball back or what?


00:08:03.197 --> 00:08:06.826
Oh, do you want this?


00:08:11.639 --> 00:08:14.904
She shoots, she scores.
Unlike you, soccer boy.


00:08:17.245 --> 00:08:20.976
Oh, so spill it. Is Luke Morgan
as hot as everyone Tweets he is?


00:08:21.149 --> 00:08:22.514
Hotter.


00:08:22.684 --> 00:08:24.311
You should ask him to the dance.


00:08:24.485 --> 00:08:26.715
Because I'm so forward with guys.


00:08:26.888 --> 00:08:29.448
First time for everything, right?


00:08:36.598 --> 00:08:38.293
- Hi, Luke.
- Hello.


00:08:38.466 --> 00:08:39.694
You have to hear my demo.


00:08:40.168 --> 00:08:43.228
It's a retro-funk-jazz explosion.


00:08:43.404 --> 00:08:45.599
Back off. I was here first.


00:08:45.773 --> 00:08:49.231
Hold on, hold up. Please hold on.
My boy does not want your demos yet.


00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:51.674
Walk away. Move along. Bye.


00:08:51.846 --> 00:08:55.213
It was nice chatting
or whatever that was.


00:08:55.483 --> 00:08:57.815
- Yes, hi, I'm, uh...
- Luke Morgan, right?


00:08:57.986 --> 00:08:59.510
Who is producing the Showcase.


00:08:59.687 --> 00:09:02.588
I don't think I'm gonna do the Showcase,
so I need to keep a low profile...


00:09:02.757 --> 00:09:06.193
Yeah, yeah. Listen close now.
There's two kinds of people in this school.


00:09:06.361 --> 00:09:09.888
There are the wannabes
and there's gonnabes.


00:09:10.064 --> 00:09:15.229
You and I, we're gonnabes. What do we do?
We stay away from the wannabes, all right?


00:09:15.403 --> 00:09:18.964
And girls named Yolanda. There are three
of them and they are certifiably...


00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:21.233
Crazy? You attract
crazy women? Shocking.


00:09:21.409 --> 00:09:24.310
It may seem like I don't have game,
but ladies love a listener.


00:09:24.479 --> 00:09:26.606
Plus, I'm telling you,
let me help you find acts.


00:09:26.781 --> 00:09:29.807
- Ah, so you're a talent scout?
- Well, bottom line, I'm a DJ.


00:09:29.984 --> 00:09:32.179
- Oh, you're a DJ as well?
- Check this.


00:09:40.728 --> 00:09:41.990
Whoa.


00:09:42.163 --> 00:09:45.257
Okay, yes. You could be very useful.
It was nice meeting you.


00:09:45.433 --> 00:09:48.095
You got a girl for the dance?
Because I can hook you up.


00:09:48.269 --> 00:09:49.429
Uh, no. Thanks.


00:09:49.604 --> 00:09:53.005
Uh, but what do you know
about Bev Van Ravensway?


00:09:53.174 --> 00:09:54.835
- Supposed to see her tonight.
- Bev?


00:09:55.009 --> 00:09:56.033
- Yeah.
- She's hot...


00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:58.678
...but the girl
is mad, mad drama, okay?


00:09:58.846 --> 00:10:01.246
I am talking to you
and you don't even know my name.


00:10:01.416 --> 00:10:03.316
- I'm Mickey O'Malley.
- Mickey O'Malley.


00:10:03.484 --> 00:10:05.111
A rarity in the Irish community.


00:10:05.687 --> 00:10:07.780
Om.


00:10:08.589 --> 00:10:11.217
RAVl: Om.
- Om.


00:10:11.392 --> 00:10:13.485
- Om.
- Om!


00:10:13.661 --> 00:10:16.186
This is not a contest, Ms. Gail.


00:10:16.564 --> 00:10:18.191
Just concentrate on your breathing.


00:10:19.701 --> 00:10:20.861
My butt is numb.


00:10:21.202 --> 00:10:24.399
If your butt is suffering,
then you are suffering.


00:10:24.572 --> 00:10:28.030
In fact, your entire life is suffering. Why?


00:10:28.209 --> 00:10:31.303
Because you crave
that which is meaningless.


00:10:31.479 --> 00:10:33.470
Are you calling me shallow?


00:10:34.549 --> 00:10:40.385
No, I'm saying to stop your craving
and release your butt.


00:10:40.555 --> 00:10:44.116
Just release it. Release it, yeah.
Release that butt.


00:10:44.992 --> 00:10:48.052
<i>Release that butt
Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:48.229 --> 00:10:50.823
<i>Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:50.998 --> 00:10:52.295
Mrs. Van Ravensway?


00:10:52.467 --> 00:10:54.992
What part
of "if you interrupt my meditation...


00:10:55.169 --> 00:10:58.366
...I will jerk your tail in a knot"
do you not understand?


00:10:58.539 --> 00:11:00.973
You told me
to tell you when dinner was ready.


00:11:01.142 --> 00:11:04.543
Oh, thank God.
I'm craving some bourbon.


00:11:08.316 --> 00:11:09.783
Victor.


00:11:09.951 --> 00:11:15.184
- Oh. Um, dinner's ready.
- Tell me something I don't know.


00:11:38.846 --> 00:11:43.283
Do you have any idea how stressful it is
to run this academy?


00:11:43.618 --> 00:11:46.109
Yes, I spent the money at the spa.


00:11:47.155 --> 00:11:49.817
<i>Five thousand dollars a night
is not very expensive...</i>


00:11:49.991 --> 00:11:54.553
<i>... when you think about the alternative,
which is me having a nervous breakdown.</i>


00:11:57.865 --> 00:11:58.889
<i>Ow.</i>


00:11:59.066 --> 00:12:01.500
<i>What are you doing?
I'm on the phone.</i>


00:12:01.669 --> 00:12:03.261
<i>- I'm cleansing.
Heh, heh.</i>


00:12:03.471 --> 00:12:05.701
Mac and cheese.


00:12:06.607 --> 00:12:09.735
<i>I don't need your spiritual counseling.</i>


00:12:10.278 --> 00:12:11.836
<i>I'm thinking of firing you.</i>


00:12:17.351 --> 00:12:20.718
Pace yourself, Ms. Gail,
or you will not be one with everything.


00:12:20.888 --> 00:12:24.221
Honey, that's what I got you for.
Now, make me one with everything.


00:12:25.626 --> 00:12:28.823
This Showcase is giving me the vapors.


00:12:28.996 --> 00:12:31.089
How did this become my life?


00:12:31.265 --> 00:12:34.257
Did I ever tell you all about the time
I nearly got my big break?


00:12:34.435 --> 00:12:35.925
Yes.
- Good.


00:12:36.103 --> 00:12:37.536
Then you all know how it goes.


00:12:37.972 --> 00:12:40.167
<i>I ain't gonna leap, I'm gonna jump</i>


00:12:40.341 --> 00:12:42.673
<i>Find my way right out of this dump</i>


00:12:45.513 --> 00:12:48.380
- I had talent, and they made me...
A laughingstock.


00:12:50.151 --> 00:12:51.448
Now look at me.


00:12:51.619 --> 00:12:54.110
I got two ungrateful kids...


00:12:54.288 --> 00:12:57.280
...a dwarfish, hairy, elfin servant...


00:12:57.458 --> 00:12:59.449
...and a random
tablecloth-wearing Asian...


00:12:59.627 --> 00:13:01.857
- Indian.
- Who makes no sense at all, ever.


00:13:02.029 --> 00:13:03.792
Why don't you have another drink, Mom.


00:13:05.333 --> 00:13:07.528
Katie, napkin me.


00:13:07.702 --> 00:13:10.193
I have got to impress Guy Morgan...


00:13:10.605 --> 00:13:13.836
...so I can stop pretending to care
about this insufferable school...


00:13:14.008 --> 00:13:17.774
...and we can all move to Hollywood where
no one pretends to care about anything.


00:13:17.945 --> 00:13:21.574
Mom, I think that you're forgetting
about the most important thing. Me.


00:13:22.516 --> 00:13:24.916
Guy will give me a deal
as soon as he hears me sing.


00:13:25.086 --> 00:13:27.680
- I doubt that.
- No, I've been practicing really hard.


00:13:27.855 --> 00:13:30.722
My voice teacher says
I've transcended to a whole new level.


00:13:30.892 --> 00:13:31.916
Yeah, I doubt it.


00:13:32.093 --> 00:13:34.653
When my first single drops,
I'll buy you that mansion...


00:13:34.829 --> 00:13:36.763
...in the Hollywood Hills...


00:13:36.931 --> 00:13:39.957
...and you can finally afford
to have your legs lengthened.


00:13:40.134 --> 00:13:42.159
- Oh, ba...
- Ms. Gail.


00:13:42.336 --> 00:13:44.304
- Miss Bev has clarity.
Katie.


00:13:44.472 --> 00:13:45.496
- You see...
- Look.


00:13:45.673 --> 00:13:49.541
- The lowly peasant tills the soil
for 40 years without any rain.


00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:53.111
But the unemployed salesman
who has recently discovered hydroponics...


00:13:53.281 --> 00:13:56.375
...all of a sudden gets disgusted by the...
- And see? No sense.


00:13:56.550 --> 00:13:58.848
- That didn't make any sense.
- Let me finish. You...


00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.954
Oh, I doubt it. You have me pray all day.


00:14:01.122 --> 00:14:03.352
- I don't feel nothing.
- You don't have a soul.


00:14:03.524 --> 00:14:06.721
No, you don't have soul.
- I have a many souls. I'll give you one.


00:14:06.894 --> 00:14:11.160
- Where's your third eye? Turn that thing on.
- I have a fourth eye too. You wanna see it?


00:14:11.332 --> 00:14:13.300
- What?
- Shh.


00:14:13.801 --> 00:14:17.328
I wanna be 6'4". Wow me, Bev.


00:14:19.874 --> 00:14:25.312
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:25.479 --> 00:14:28.039
Just stop. Stop the wowing, okay?


00:14:28.215 --> 00:14:30.308
What's wrong?
- Somehow you've gotten worse.


00:14:30.484 --> 00:14:32.213
I don't know how that was possible...


00:14:32.386 --> 00:14:35.014
...but there isn't enough Auto-Tune
that's gonna fix you.


00:14:35.189 --> 00:14:38.522
- Well, Katie's bad playing threw me off.
- I don't think it was that.


00:14:38.693 --> 00:14:40.320
Again.


00:14:40.494 --> 00:14:42.052
Really? Okay.


00:14:42.229 --> 00:14:47.861
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:48.035 --> 00:14:49.161
Ouch.


00:14:49.337 --> 00:14:52.397
I could belch the song better.


00:14:54.008 --> 00:14:56.169
Have you been drinking
the floor wax again?


00:14:56.344 --> 00:14:57.811
Anything to forget I live here.


00:14:57.979 --> 00:15:00.880
Ugh. My head is buzzing
like a skeeter on a septic tank.


00:15:01.048 --> 00:15:04.950
- Ravi, meditate me.
Good luck, buddy.


00:15:05.319 --> 00:15:08.982
Well, it doesn't matter,
because I have my own plan.


00:15:13.194 --> 00:15:15.560
Does it make me a bad person
that I kind of enjoyed that?


00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:17.459
No.


00:15:17.631 --> 00:15:19.929
Hmm. Nice work.


00:15:32.113 --> 00:15:35.412
- Guess who's on his way over.
- Not now, Victor, I'm busy.


00:15:35.583 --> 00:15:38.051
Guess or prepare to get creamed.


00:15:48.529 --> 00:15:51.623
Victor! Victor! Victor, stop!


00:15:56.504 --> 00:15:58.233
<i>I've got rings on my fingers</i>


00:15:58.406 --> 00:15:59.498
<i>And glitter in my hair</i>


00:15:59.673 --> 00:16:03.769
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:16:03.944 --> 00:16:05.275
<i>I'm gonna run...</i>


00:16:05.446 --> 00:16:08.210
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Victor, what are you doing?


00:16:08.649 --> 00:16:09.946
Victor!


00:16:10.117 --> 00:16:13.348
Victor, where did you put my clothes?


00:16:13.521 --> 00:16:15.682
- Surprise!
- What? No.


00:16:19.193 --> 00:16:20.820
I'm gonna kill you. Victor!


00:16:30.738 --> 00:16:31.898
Oh, hi, Katie.


00:16:32.073 --> 00:16:33.472
You are evil. Let me in.


00:16:33.641 --> 00:16:37.077
I control every lock on this property.


00:16:37.244 --> 00:16:38.905
Crap.


00:16:42.316 --> 00:16:44.011
This is insane.


00:16:44.185 --> 00:16:48.246
Yeah, try the shed, it's unlocked, idiot.


00:16:58.032 --> 00:17:00.125
You gotta be kidding me.


00:17:01.869 --> 00:17:03.496
Crap.


00:17:06.807 --> 00:17:10.402
How did such an untalented daughter
spring from my loins?


00:17:10.578 --> 00:17:14.378
Focus, Ms. Gail. We are making
an offering to your personal deity.


00:17:14.548 --> 00:17:16.675
Tell him to give me fame and fortune.


00:17:16.851 --> 00:17:18.546
Not exactly how it works.


00:17:18.719 --> 00:17:21.279
<i>Now, breathe through your Mula Bandha.</i>


00:17:21.455 --> 00:17:24.515
Oh, honey, if I could do that,
I'd get a million hits on YouTube.


00:17:24.692 --> 00:17:26.922
How much longer is this gonna take?
Ugh.


00:17:27.094 --> 00:17:29.221
The prayer or the fame and fortune?


00:17:31.565 --> 00:17:33.032
Ha, ha. See you later.


00:17:39.206 --> 00:17:41.071
Victor.


00:17:44.912 --> 00:17:46.345
Katie?


00:17:47.548 --> 00:17:49.778
- Luke.
- Katie.


00:17:49.984 --> 00:17:53.249
- Are you wearing a doormat?
- Yes.


00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:56.184
- Welcome.
- Why, thank you.


00:17:57.224 --> 00:17:59.055
The truth. Um...


00:18:00.361 --> 00:18:03.694
My stepbrother locked me
outside of the house.


00:18:03.864 --> 00:18:05.195
Naked.


00:18:06.233 --> 00:18:08.531
Oh, sorry. You should...
You should take my jacket.


00:18:08.702 --> 00:18:10.226
Oh.
- Oh, no, no.


00:18:12.673 --> 00:18:13.765
There.


00:18:13.941 --> 00:18:17.138
- Thanks. Now the pants.
- Hmm?


00:18:21.749 --> 00:18:23.376
I'm kidding.


00:18:23.918 --> 00:18:25.749
- You got me.
- Ha, ha.


00:18:26.086 --> 00:18:27.110
No, no.


00:18:27.288 --> 00:18:30.689
One more parent-teacher conference,
I swear I'm gonna lose it.


00:18:30.858 --> 00:18:33.053
Look at me. I'm an educator.


00:18:33.661 --> 00:18:38.325
I have no real skills. And I will die
before I go back to my daddy's farm.


00:18:38.832 --> 00:18:42.632
You tell my personal deity
to help me achieve Guy Morgan. Do it.


00:18:42.803 --> 00:18:45.397
I'll put another banana on the altar.


00:18:49.276 --> 00:18:50.937
What is that?


00:18:51.512 --> 00:18:53.776
Do you hear angels singing?


00:18:53.948 --> 00:18:55.916
Perhaps the gods
have answered your prayer.


00:18:57.117 --> 00:18:58.846
Hey. What...?


00:19:11.699 --> 00:19:14.190
<i>- This is Gail Van Ravensway.
Hello.</i>


00:19:14.368 --> 00:19:15.995
Guy Morgan here. How are you?


00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:18.297
Oh, well, hello, Guy.


00:19:18.472 --> 00:19:20.736
What a surprise
to see you calling this number.


00:19:20.908 --> 00:19:21.932
Do you hear this?


00:19:22.109 --> 00:19:23.770
<i>I can justify</i>


00:19:23.944 --> 00:19:25.639
That's the demo your girl, Katie...


00:19:25.813 --> 00:19:28.145
<i>... slipped into my briefcase.</i>


00:19:28.315 --> 00:19:30.510
And it sounds like money, dear.


00:19:30.684 --> 00:19:32.549
She gave you a CD?


00:19:32.720 --> 00:19:36.087
Oh, well. Well, ain't that the berries.


00:19:37.324 --> 00:19:41.192
Ravi, what frigging god did you pray to?


00:19:42.429 --> 00:19:46.525
Guy, yeah, it seems someone's
not being entirely honest here.


00:19:48.502 --> 00:19:50.697
Katie, somebody get that door!


00:19:51.839 --> 00:19:53.397
So...


00:19:54.275 --> 00:19:56.402
...that meeting today...


00:19:56.577 --> 00:19:59.375
...it was obvious
that your dad doesn't get you.


00:19:59.713 --> 00:20:01.772
He's an idiot for not liking your music.


00:20:01.949 --> 00:20:04.383
Well, it's... It's complicated.


00:20:04.652 --> 00:20:05.846
I'm gonna just, uh...


00:20:07.321 --> 00:20:09.221
Is it as complicated as me...


00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:12.518
...getting stuck outside
in only a welcome mat?


00:20:12.793 --> 00:20:16.524
That's not complicated.
That is a gift from God.


00:20:21.435 --> 00:20:24.233
Luke. Katie. What are you doing?


00:20:24.405 --> 00:20:27.465
Well, it seems your brother
is Satan's very own personal Mini-Me.


00:20:27.641 --> 00:20:29.905
Oh, I know, tell me about it. Come on in.


00:20:33.881 --> 00:20:35.542
Oh, my God, did you work out today?


00:20:37.217 --> 00:20:38.514
- Sit down.
- Ooh, look at this.


00:20:38.686 --> 00:20:41.780
- Ha, ha. Some lemonade.
- Why, thank you.


00:20:41.955 --> 00:20:44.423
You know, my stepsister,
she has body issues...


00:20:44.591 --> 00:20:46.752
...so I don't like
to discourage her nudity.


00:20:46.927 --> 00:20:48.121
That's interesting.


00:20:48.295 --> 00:20:51.059
- She's absolutely lovely...
- Would you like an appetizer?


00:20:51.231 --> 00:20:52.459
<i>Oh, fromage.</i>


00:20:52.633 --> 00:20:54.260
I only have cheese.


00:20:57.438 --> 00:20:59.406
I just got off the phone
with Guy Morgan.


00:20:59.573 --> 00:21:01.473
Your phone.


00:21:04.511 --> 00:21:07.378
He just loved that little demo
you left him.


00:21:07.548 --> 00:21:09.106
I have underestimated you.


00:21:09.683 --> 00:21:11.514
It'd make me proud
if I cared about you.


00:21:11.685 --> 00:21:14.779
- I didn't lie about anything.
- Oh, but, chicken, you did.


00:21:14.955 --> 00:21:17.583
At least that's what Guy thinks,
now that I've clarified.


00:21:17.758 --> 00:21:21.956
I told him it was Bev's demo
and that you stole it from her.


00:21:22.129 --> 00:21:25.394
- But you can't do that. That's my song.
- It's Bev's song.


00:21:25.566 --> 00:21:29.002
And Guy can't wait to see her perform it
at the Showcase.


00:21:29.169 --> 00:21:32.297
If you try to contact him, I'll deny
everything and lock you in the basement.


00:21:32.473 --> 00:21:37.604
- She can't sing to save her life.
- No, but you can, can't you?


00:21:38.879 --> 00:21:41.040
Now, let's hear this amazing voice.


00:21:46.453 --> 00:21:51.083
<i>Like a malignant tumor
She's got no sense of humor</i>


00:21:51.258 --> 00:21:55.354
<i>Just like a swollen blister
It's best to just resist her</i>


00:21:55.529 --> 00:21:59.295
<i>She's not exactly a witch
She's just a terrible bi...</i>


00:21:59.767 --> 00:22:01.428
Well, your lyrics stink.


00:22:01.602 --> 00:22:03.763
But Guy's right, you've got chops.


00:22:07.007 --> 00:22:09.703
Do you know what other instruments
I'm good at?


00:22:10.277 --> 00:22:13.735
I have a feeling I could get in trouble
with a question like that.


00:22:14.181 --> 00:22:16.149
I like trouble.


00:22:17.684 --> 00:22:18.810
Hey, kids.


00:22:20.120 --> 00:22:23.556
- Good evening, Miss Van Ravensway.
- Sorry, I need you to go. Now.


00:22:23.724 --> 00:22:26.488
Family emergency. I need Bev
to help me pass a kidney stone.


00:22:26.660 --> 00:22:30.494
- So she had a lovely evening. Ta-ta.
- Are you trying to ruin my life?


00:22:30.798 --> 00:22:36.031
I have figured out a way for you
to wow Guy Morgan in the Showcase.


00:22:36.236 --> 00:22:38.704
- So you do think I've improved?
- Oh, no, honey.


00:22:38.972 --> 00:22:41.532
But my month of spiritual devotion
has taught me...


00:22:41.708 --> 00:22:43.676
...that God works in annoying ways.


00:22:43.844 --> 00:22:46.904
How am I to wow Guy Morgan
if I supposedly can't sing?


00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:50.140
You can't, but Katie can.


00:22:50.317 --> 00:22:53.013
- What?
- I know. Like I said, annoying.


00:22:53.187 --> 00:22:56.486
We'll record her voice
and you will lip synch.


00:22:56.657 --> 00:22:58.488
What if I don't want to?


00:22:59.593 --> 00:23:03.324
Don't you get snarky with me,
you ungrateful toad.


00:23:03.497 --> 00:23:05.556
- I saved your life.
- You didn't do anything.


00:23:05.732 --> 00:23:07.996
- My dad married you.
- Yeah, and then he died.


00:23:08.168 --> 00:23:11.729
I tried to put you in foster care,
but they was all fulled up on ugly.


00:23:11.905 --> 00:23:13.395
- Funny.
- I thought it was...


00:23:13.574 --> 00:23:15.041
...because you don't wanna look bad.


00:23:16.643 --> 00:23:18.770
Katie, if you don't sing...


00:23:18.946 --> 00:23:22.074
...I'm gonna find a way for that savings
your dad left to disappear.


00:23:22.483 --> 00:23:26.681
That means, you forget college,
moving out, you're stuck here with me.


00:23:26.854 --> 00:23:30.688
But, pumpkin, we're gonna have
so much fun growing old together.


00:23:30.858 --> 00:23:33.759
Why don't you just have her perform
if you like her so much?


00:23:33.927 --> 00:23:36.191
Because, honey, look at you.


00:23:36.363 --> 00:23:38.490
You are a star.


00:23:38.665 --> 00:23:42.863
That is what Guy Morgan needs.
You, the star.


00:23:43.036 --> 00:23:44.594
I'm a star.


00:23:44.771 --> 00:23:48.935
- A bright, gassy star.
- Yes, you are.


00:23:49.109 --> 00:23:51.509
And Guy Morgan is gonna
give you a swimming pool...


00:23:51.678 --> 00:23:53.646
...shaped just like Colin Farrell.


00:23:53.814 --> 00:23:55.372
Every part of him.


00:23:55.549 --> 00:23:59.076
Or, Bev, you could just see every part
of Colin Farrell on the Internet.


00:23:59.253 --> 00:24:02.017
And just leave me out of this.


00:24:03.290 --> 00:24:05.850
- Okay, so how do we do this?
- First rule of Lie Club...


00:24:06.026 --> 00:24:07.926
...is don't talk about Lie Club.


00:24:08.529 --> 00:24:10.429
Which includes you, Katie.


00:24:10.597 --> 00:24:13.293
As far as everyone knows,
you can't sing.


00:24:13.467 --> 00:24:15.526
And no more talking to Luke or Guy.


00:24:15.702 --> 00:24:17.067
Are we clear?


00:24:17.504 --> 00:24:18.698
Crystal.


00:24:20.641 --> 00:24:23.633
Yeah, Dad, we're about to meet
some fresh talent right now.


00:24:23.810 --> 00:24:27.803
Remember when you signed Jay-Z?
No, you passed on him, my bad.


00:24:27.981 --> 00:24:30.449
Um, this is like that,
except it's gonna be brilliant.


00:24:30.617 --> 00:24:31.948
Yeah. Okay.


00:24:32.119 --> 00:24:34.246
- Yeah, okay. Bye.
- Dude, what'd he say?


00:24:34.421 --> 00:24:35.945
These guys you told me about are good?


00:24:36.123 --> 00:24:39.490
Yes. The Oral Majority has potential.
They'll be here any second.


00:24:39.660 --> 00:24:42.356
Talking about potential,
how was your little date with Bev?


00:24:42.529 --> 00:24:44.793
- Her mom kicked me out.
- I told you. Bev is drama.


00:24:44.965 --> 00:24:46.523
Technically, it was Gail's drama.


00:24:46.700 --> 00:24:48.827
But Bev's interesting, man. She's...


00:24:49.002 --> 00:24:50.469
I'm worried she's bonkers.


00:24:50.637 --> 00:24:53.470
See, my last girlfriend, she was hot,
but absolutely mental.


00:24:53.640 --> 00:24:56.302
I need a girl who's not gonna be
shipped to the loony bin.


00:24:56.476 --> 00:24:58.239
Hang on, I'm gonna hit the facilities.


00:24:58.412 --> 00:25:00.107
Facilities. That's a new one.


00:25:00.547 --> 00:25:03.243
- Hey, man. Sorry we're late.
- Hey, what's good, y'all?


00:25:03.417 --> 00:25:06.147
Nobody talks to my boy
until he comes from the facilities.


00:25:06.320 --> 00:25:07.514
We're here to impress.


00:25:07.688 --> 00:25:09.952
- Clear, right?
- Got it.


00:25:13.794 --> 00:25:16.262
<i>When you're fighting just to keep it sane</i>


00:25:16.430 --> 00:25:18.694
<i>Throw your will
At the eye of the hurricane</i>


00:25:18.865 --> 00:25:21.060
<i>- Sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:21.234 --> 00:25:24.601
<i>- Help me sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:24.771 --> 00:25:27.296
<i>If you wanna find out who you are
Stop running</i>


00:25:27.474 --> 00:25:30.739
<i>In the end you'll figure out
It's all about nothing</i>


00:25:30.911 --> 00:25:36.213
<i>All night, it's gonna be all right
Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>


00:25:36.383 --> 00:25:43.118
<i>All right
Turn your dreams into your life</i>


00:25:44.324 --> 00:25:45.814
That's good.


00:25:52.866 --> 00:25:56.165
I'm clean. No one followed me.
And I got your intel.


00:25:57.004 --> 00:25:59.336
Oh, Katie, baby, your life sucks.


00:25:59.506 --> 00:26:01.406
Trust me, it gets worse.


00:26:02.442 --> 00:26:06.037
Okay, dude, those guys, they
just went Oral Majority on me in there...


00:26:06.213 --> 00:26:08.408
- I was trying to hold them back...
- You're right.


00:26:08.582 --> 00:26:10.516
They have potential and they're great.


00:26:10.684 --> 00:26:15.917
But first, my talent-finding friend,
promise me no more auditions in the bogs.


00:26:16.089 --> 00:26:18.284
- The what?
- The loo.


00:26:18.825 --> 00:26:20.588
- Bathroom. Toilet.
- Got it.


00:26:20.761 --> 00:26:23.355
All right. Okay, come on.
I wanna show you something.


00:26:23.964 --> 00:26:27.263
So now I have to rehearse in secret.


00:26:27.434 --> 00:26:28.901
Why not not rehearse?


00:26:29.069 --> 00:26:31.094
Make Bev sound bad. What do you care?


00:26:31.271 --> 00:26:34.263
No song, no savings account. No life.


00:26:36.443 --> 00:26:38.877
People. Coming. Now.


00:26:42.416 --> 00:26:44.247
Okay.


00:26:44.818 --> 00:26:47.184
Dude, what are we doing?
The suspense is killing me.


00:26:47.521 --> 00:26:49.284
Can you grab the mike?


00:26:49.456 --> 00:26:51.447
Not about to serenade
a brother, are you?


00:26:51.625 --> 00:26:53.456
Dude, with bromance, comes a fine line.


00:26:53.627 --> 00:26:55.925
That I shall not cross.


00:26:56.396 --> 00:26:58.694
So sing something.


00:27:00.367 --> 00:27:01.834
Okay.


00:27:05.972 --> 00:27:08.770
<i>I'm lost in a world
That rattles my brain</i>


00:27:08.942 --> 00:27:11.433
<i>I'm cleaning up my life
From the mess you made</i>


00:27:11.611 --> 00:27:13.010
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:13.480 --> 00:27:15.471
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:17.284 --> 00:27:19.752
<i>My soul's in debt, but my bills are paid</i>


00:27:19.920 --> 00:27:22.445
<i>I'd give anything just to make an escape</i>


00:27:22.622 --> 00:27:24.214
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:24.725 --> 00:27:26.352
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:27.360 --> 00:27:30.295
<i>So you can keep
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:30.464 --> 00:27:32.796
<i>Baby, you're rockin'
But there ain't no way I'm ever letting you in</i>


00:27:32.966 --> 00:27:34.433
<i>He's amazing.</i>


00:27:35.836 --> 00:27:37.497
<i>Not again</i>


00:27:38.438 --> 00:27:41.271
<i>So keep on
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:41.441 --> 00:27:46.640
<i>But, baby, you're better off walking
'Cause I ain't gonna let you in</i>


00:27:46.813 --> 00:27:48.371
<i>Never again</i>


00:27:49.483 --> 00:27:52.077
<i>I went out on a limb again</i>


00:27:52.252 --> 00:27:54.812
<i>I guess I had to lose to win</i>


00:27:54.988 --> 00:27:59.357
<i>I was too confused to know
Which way to turn</i>


00:28:00.761 --> 00:28:03.423
<i>- And she could be a millionaire...
- Crap.</i>


00:28:03.597 --> 00:28:05.861
<i>- Gail needs me to drive her home.
- I don't care</i>


00:28:06.032 --> 00:28:08.694
<i>'Cause, baby, there's nobody home</i>


00:28:08.869 --> 00:28:11.360
<i>Nobody's home at all, yeah</i>


00:28:15.842 --> 00:28:17.969
- What? Did you write that?
- Yeah.


00:28:18.145 --> 00:28:20.773
Reminds me of, um... Uh...


00:28:20.947 --> 00:28:24.280
- Danger Fruit, right? Danger Fruit.
- Ha, ha. Because I wrote their album too.


00:28:24.551 --> 00:28:27.042
Shut up. Took me forever
to find that bootleg online.


00:28:27.220 --> 00:28:29.211
- I love that album. That's crazy.
- Yeah.


00:28:29.389 --> 00:28:31.687
My dad doesn't know.
And he thought the record...


00:28:31.858 --> 00:28:33.553
...was a pile of crap.


00:28:33.827 --> 00:28:35.522
He thinks writing's a waste of time.


00:28:35.962 --> 00:28:39.796
Because he basically wants me
to be like him. Only with better hair.


00:28:40.267 --> 00:28:44.363
But the first thing I thought when
I heard those guys in the urinals was...


00:28:44.538 --> 00:28:45.562
...good acoustics.


00:28:45.972 --> 00:28:49.806
Second thought was these guys,
these guys could be great.


00:28:49.976 --> 00:28:51.568
If you gave them your song.


00:28:52.979 --> 00:28:54.640
Mate, that's a brilliant idea.


00:28:55.382 --> 00:28:58.078
- So put them in the Showcase?
- Put them in the Showcase.


00:28:58.251 --> 00:28:59.582
Yeah.


00:29:01.254 --> 00:29:07.784
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:29:08.094 --> 00:29:09.391
You wrote that song today?


00:29:09.563 --> 00:29:13.021
- You've been home for what, two hours?
- It's like an answer to his song.


00:29:13.300 --> 00:29:14.597
You really like this guy.


00:29:14.768 --> 00:29:16.463
Yeah, I'm an idiot.


00:29:16.636 --> 00:29:18.831
You have to sing that for him.


00:29:19.005 --> 00:29:22.497
What if you sang to him in secret?


00:29:24.311 --> 00:29:27.109
At the dance. Ta-da.


00:29:30.717 --> 00:29:33.550
Okay, I know the card's
like, really cheesy, but...


00:29:35.589 --> 00:29:38.057
Oh, God, I hope you like it.


00:29:38.391 --> 00:29:41.883
Ange, it's beautiful,
but are you crazy?


00:29:42.062 --> 00:29:44.087
No, I know you're crazy.


00:29:44.264 --> 00:29:45.288
Am not.


00:29:46.333 --> 00:29:49.325
- What if he doesn't even like me?
- You'll both be in disguise.


00:29:49.502 --> 00:29:52.198
It's your chance to see
if he was really flirting with you.


00:29:52.372 --> 00:29:54.932
I was naked. Of course he was flirting.


00:29:55.108 --> 00:29:57.804
And why even torture myself?
It's not like I can have him.


00:29:57.978 --> 00:29:59.912
Why not? Tell him how you feel.


00:30:00.080 --> 00:30:04.107
If he feels the same way, you can reveal
your hot self and he won't tell Gail.


00:30:04.484 --> 00:30:07.578
And if he hates the song,
leave the disguise on.


00:30:10.523 --> 00:30:12.047
Okay.


00:30:12.359 --> 00:30:13.951
I'm going to the dance.


00:30:14.127 --> 00:30:15.458
That's my girl.


00:30:15.729 --> 00:30:19.722
<i>Maurice, no, no.
Again, in Français, longer legs.</i>


00:30:19.900 --> 00:30:23.199
I wouldn't go in your closet
for a little while if I were you.


00:30:23.370 --> 00:30:25.133
What? Why?


00:30:25.305 --> 00:30:26.670
Hey. Wake up.


00:30:30.577 --> 00:30:32.135
Katie!


00:30:32.312 --> 00:30:35.748
The cat has pooped in my closet.
I need you to clean it up.


00:30:35.916 --> 00:30:37.406
Go.


00:30:37.584 --> 00:30:39.313
I told you we don't have a cat.


00:30:39.486 --> 00:30:40.817
Angie, heads up.


00:30:42.789 --> 00:30:44.086
Katie!


00:30:49.296 --> 00:30:51.025
What's going on?


00:30:51.197 --> 00:30:52.630
Nothing.


00:30:52.799 --> 00:30:55.927
I am, uh, re-organizing and labeling. I...


00:30:56.102 --> 00:30:58.400
I took up crochet.
Do you want new socks?


00:30:58.571 --> 00:31:02.632
I would make you a sweater, but I hear
that the arms, that they're really hard.


00:31:05.879 --> 00:31:10.043
Oh, you thought you could sneak off
and go to the dance.


00:31:10.216 --> 00:31:12.446
After what you pulled today with Guy.


00:31:12.619 --> 00:31:14.052
Oh, no, no.


00:31:14.220 --> 00:31:16.711
Oh, no, no, no.


00:31:16.890 --> 00:31:19.188
You're on Victor watch tonight...


00:31:19.359 --> 00:31:22.055
...tomorrow night and every night.


00:31:22.228 --> 00:31:23.252
Fun.


00:31:23.430 --> 00:31:26.558
I'll give Victor all the mothering
you don't have time for.


00:31:26.733 --> 00:31:30.134
Oh, I wish you could be my mommy.


00:31:31.004 --> 00:31:33.029
I'm off to my cinnamon colonic.


00:31:37.010 --> 00:31:39.376
Hey. Get down.
You're gonna break yourself.


00:31:39.713 --> 00:31:41.977
Or worse, the furniture.


00:31:42.282 --> 00:31:45.376
Hello?
- Hey.


00:31:45.652 --> 00:31:48.815
- You look like you're having fun.
- Always.


00:31:49.155 --> 00:31:52.215
Well, I couldn't let you not go to the dance
without me.


00:31:52.392 --> 00:31:54.792
Besides, we have six hours
of shirtless Team Jacob.


00:31:54.961 --> 00:31:57.896
So let's just get this party started.


00:31:58.064 --> 00:32:02.091
- So is Victor driving you nuts?
- I swear to you, he's not human.


00:32:02.369 --> 00:32:05.668
I mean, can you really blame him, though?
Just look at this family.


00:32:06.873 --> 00:32:08.170
Victor, what are you doing?


00:32:18.151 --> 00:32:20.415
Oh, no. Great.


00:32:20.587 --> 00:32:22.782
Eh, she actually looks prettier
that way.


00:32:23.390 --> 00:32:26.416
True. Ugh. Whatever.


00:32:27.594 --> 00:32:30.722
Why did I ever think that tonight
could've been something special.


00:32:31.498 --> 00:32:33.762
Think Bev's all over Luke at the dance
right now?


00:32:33.933 --> 00:32:36.231
They're probably making out. See?


00:32:36.403 --> 00:32:39.600
- Victor, give it a rest.
- Just check it out. Come on.


00:32:42.809 --> 00:32:45.437
<i>Luke is gonna produce
whoever wins the Showcase.</i>


00:32:45.612 --> 00:32:48.672
<i>So we need a little insurance.</i>


00:32:48.848 --> 00:32:52.045
<i>- I know what I'm doing, Mother.
Do you?</i>


00:32:52.952 --> 00:32:55.819
I can't take it anymore, okay?


00:32:55.989 --> 00:32:58.048
I'm taking my life into my own hands.


00:32:58.224 --> 00:32:59.316
I'm talking to Luke.


00:32:59.926 --> 00:33:02.417
- Finally.
- Okay, but we have gotta be home...


00:33:02.595 --> 00:33:04.062
...before Gail gets here.


00:33:04.798 --> 00:33:06.129
What about the demon spawn?


00:33:06.299 --> 00:33:07.323
Mm-hm.


00:33:07.500 --> 00:33:08.899
Right.


00:33:09.903 --> 00:33:11.302
Okay, just watch him.


00:33:14.374 --> 00:33:15.636
Hmm.


00:33:20.447 --> 00:33:22.438
Is that all you've got, Angela?


00:33:23.116 --> 00:33:24.140
Ravi?


00:33:25.819 --> 00:33:28.344
My sister could catch that, jerknut.


00:33:28.521 --> 00:33:30.955
Put some nuts in that sack, ref.


00:33:33.093 --> 00:33:35.653
Miss Katie, I am most startled.


00:33:35.829 --> 00:33:37.023
Obviously.


00:33:37.564 --> 00:33:40.055
All right. All right. Don't hate me.


00:33:40.233 --> 00:33:41.791
Okay, don't hate me. I'm sorry.


00:33:41.968 --> 00:33:45.335
But my name ain't Ravi. It's Tony.


00:33:45.872 --> 00:33:49.000
- Tony.
- Tony Gupta from Jersey.


00:33:49.175 --> 00:33:51.837
- From Jersey.
- I am half Indian.


00:33:52.212 --> 00:33:55.613
My friends call me Meatball
because I'm half Italian.


00:33:55.782 --> 00:33:57.647
Truth is I always wanted to be an actor.


00:33:58.017 --> 00:33:59.541
But I never got my shot.


00:33:59.719 --> 00:34:01.949
I'm working at KFC,
and one day, Gail comes in...


00:34:02.122 --> 00:34:04.522
...she's like, "Are you Indian?"
I'm like, "What?"


00:34:04.691 --> 00:34:06.886
She's like, "Are you a guru?"
I'm like:


00:34:07.060 --> 00:34:08.550
"Who is asking?"


00:34:08.828 --> 00:34:12.195
She says, "Someone
who's paying for some spiritual guidance."


00:34:12.365 --> 00:34:14.959
And I'm like, "Whaa! It's a miracle!"


00:34:15.135 --> 00:34:19.504
I finally get a chance to do
a total immersion into a character.


00:34:19.806 --> 00:34:22.070
Real training and I get paid.
Are you kidding me?


00:34:22.242 --> 00:34:24.642
Ravi is my King Lear.


00:34:24.978 --> 00:34:27.606
<i>You wanna hear
the monologue from My Fair Lady?</i>


00:34:27.780 --> 00:34:28.974
- Oy, mate.
- No, thanks.


00:34:30.183 --> 00:34:32.879
I'm sorry I barged in. Whoops.


00:34:35.688 --> 00:34:39.351
Your secret's safe with me, okay?
But I need to ask you a favor.


00:34:40.026 --> 00:34:42.085
- Meatball.
- Ha, Meatball.


00:34:42.262 --> 00:34:44.730
Please watch Victor tonight
so I can go to the dance?


00:34:44.898 --> 00:34:45.956
Are you kidding me? Done.


00:34:47.534 --> 00:34:48.865
Blow it up.


00:34:50.803 --> 00:34:52.361
Thank you.


00:35:02.182 --> 00:35:03.581
Whoa.


00:35:03.750 --> 00:35:06.378
How am I supposed to find Luke
if everybody's got a mask?


00:35:06.553 --> 00:35:09.613
I never said this was
gonna be easy. Let's do some recon.


00:35:10.990 --> 00:35:13.322
I am Assistant Principal
Dorothy Plumberg.


00:35:13.493 --> 00:35:16.724
No drinking. No texting. No kissing.


00:35:19.432 --> 00:35:22.401
Luke? No. Luke Morgan?


00:35:22.569 --> 00:35:26.198
No leaving the premises
and no experiencing joy of any kind.


00:35:26.906 --> 00:35:29.238
Luke? Ugh.


00:35:34.614 --> 00:35:36.047
Where is he?


00:35:36.883 --> 00:35:39.681
That reminds me.
I got a new act for you to listen to.


00:35:39.852 --> 00:35:41.513
- Now?
- No time like it.


00:35:41.688 --> 00:35:44.122
- Dude, not again...
- We're called Big Pain Ticket.


00:35:47.627 --> 00:35:51.188
<i>I wanna kiss your apocalypse</i>


00:35:51.364 --> 00:35:54.697
<i>Wrap you in my Armageddon</i>


00:35:54.867 --> 00:35:57.062
<i>Sing you a twisted serenade</i>


00:35:57.270 --> 00:36:00.000
They're good, but I'm worried
that chain saw's unsafe.


00:36:00.173 --> 00:36:02.607
Dude, the chain saw's,
like, the best part.


00:36:09.415 --> 00:36:10.473
I think I found him.


00:36:10.650 --> 00:36:12.914
Well, he is blond.


00:36:16.022 --> 00:36:18.320
Oh, my God, what is she doing here?


00:36:20.226 --> 00:36:22.524
I hate teenage desperation.


00:36:22.695 --> 00:36:24.094
What are you doing here?


00:36:24.264 --> 00:36:27.097
Oh, honey, the prize pig
doesn't win the blue ribbon...


00:36:27.267 --> 00:36:29.292
...by covering up its third best asset.


00:36:29.469 --> 00:36:32.404
A, what does that even mean
and, B, did you just call me a pig?


00:36:32.572 --> 00:36:34.403
Honey, I saw you making sweet love...


00:36:34.574 --> 00:36:37.042
...to a plate of Swedish meatballs
at the snack table.


00:36:39.479 --> 00:36:41.606
It's now or never, babe.


00:36:43.149 --> 00:36:46.585
- What if she recognizes me?
- I'll distract her. Go.


00:36:46.753 --> 00:36:48.948
- So was I right or was I right?
- You were right.


00:36:49.122 --> 00:36:51.989
You have very cool taste.
Any more auditions in the men's...


00:36:52.158 --> 00:36:54.092
...and you're fired.


00:36:57.130 --> 00:37:00.657
- I know your secret.
- Which secret is that?


00:37:03.269 --> 00:37:04.759
I heard you sing at school.


00:37:05.004 --> 00:37:06.130
You were amazing.


00:37:06.306 --> 00:37:07.364
Do I know you?


00:37:11.711 --> 00:37:14.305
- I wanna show you something.
- What's your name?


00:37:16.649 --> 00:37:18.708
Angela, what are you doing?


00:37:19.352 --> 00:37:21.843
I'd like to make a request.


00:37:26.359 --> 00:37:29.192
I will make your night. I promise.


00:37:29.362 --> 00:37:30.727
Miss Van R.


00:37:31.364 --> 00:37:33.764
Is it true you wanted to be a dancer
when you were younger...


00:37:33.933 --> 00:37:35.127
...but were never good enough?


00:37:36.502 --> 00:37:38.163
Who told you that?


00:37:55.888 --> 00:37:57.321
Well, now, how lovely.


00:37:57.490 --> 00:38:00.687
But I've seen better dancing
in a Filipino prison, sugar.


00:38:00.860 --> 00:38:01.986
Oh!


00:38:02.161 --> 00:38:06.393
Really? Because I think
I just challenged you to a dance battle.


00:38:10.737 --> 00:38:13.831
Would Luke Morgan please pick up
the white courtesy phone?


00:38:14.006 --> 00:38:16.907
Luke Morgan, white courtesy phone.


00:38:21.681 --> 00:38:24.411
Hold on. What is that?
You've never seen a guitar before?


00:38:24.751 --> 00:38:27.447
You hid a guitar in there.
You hiding anything else?


00:38:27.620 --> 00:38:28.882
Follow me.


00:38:33.926 --> 00:38:35.757
Oh, wow.


00:38:38.231 --> 00:38:43.794
Madam, while your exquisite eyes
tell of a radiant, but mischievous beauty...


00:38:44.670 --> 00:38:46.570
...I have grown impatient.


00:38:46.739 --> 00:38:50.436
Off with your veil,
so that I may know the truth.


00:38:51.944 --> 00:38:53.138
Or not.


00:38:55.415 --> 00:38:58.441
I'm hoping this answers
a lot of your questions.


00:39:04.657 --> 00:39:08.218
<i>I can see it from the spark in your eyes</i>


00:39:09.529 --> 00:39:13.761
<i>You believe in all the things
You've denied</i>


00:39:13.933 --> 00:39:17.460
<i>You wanna fly
And leave your worries behind</i>


00:39:17.637 --> 00:39:21.630
<i>Don't you? Don't you?</i>


00:39:23.609 --> 00:39:26.942
<i>Well, now I'm knocking
At your front door</i>


00:39:28.714 --> 00:39:32.411
<i>And I'm looking for the right cure</i>


00:39:33.085 --> 00:39:36.782
<i>I'm still a little bit unsure</i>


00:39:37.256 --> 00:39:40.089
Okay, now take off that veil.


00:39:40.560 --> 00:39:41.652
Uh-uh.


00:42:20.586 --> 00:42:23.180
I think I've blown something.


00:42:23.356 --> 00:42:26.416
Does anyone else smell cinnamon?


00:42:29.028 --> 00:42:30.586
Move it, fatso.


00:42:32.331 --> 00:42:38.930
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:42:39.672 --> 00:42:43.301
Okay, you are blowing my mind.
You have to show me who you are.


00:42:55.855 --> 00:42:57.288
- We have to go.
- What?


00:42:57.456 --> 00:42:59.481
- Come.
- No, Ange.


00:42:59.659 --> 00:43:02.219
In the middle of a really big moment
right now.


00:43:02.395 --> 00:43:04.363
Someone had an accident
and went home.


00:43:06.832 --> 00:43:08.197
I'm so sorry.


00:43:08.901 --> 00:43:10.129
What...? You...?


00:43:10.836 --> 00:43:12.497
Hey. Wait.


00:43:12.672 --> 00:43:13.900
But who are you?


00:43:14.073 --> 00:43:16.667
Over here. Go, go, go.


00:43:24.817 --> 00:43:27.843
- We beat her.
- I love you for this.


00:43:46.305 --> 00:43:48.330
Interesting babysitting attire.


00:43:49.108 --> 00:43:52.043
I should've known
you'd go behind my back again.


00:43:52.478 --> 00:43:55.413
And that Paula Abdul wannabe,
trying to distract me.


00:43:55.748 --> 00:43:57.943
Don't talk about her like that.


00:43:59.952 --> 00:44:03.115
Your friend wants to be a choreographer,
if memory serves.


00:44:03.289 --> 00:44:06.850
She might've made a decent one
if she hadn't gotten herself expelled.


00:44:07.026 --> 00:44:09.290
Guess she can kiss
them Juilliard dreams goodbye.


00:44:09.462 --> 00:44:12.522
Look, I'll do whatever you want.
Okay? Just leave Ange out of this.


00:44:12.832 --> 00:44:15.960
That depends if you pull another stunt
like tonight, sugar.


00:44:16.869 --> 00:44:19.997
- I won't.
- I'll be taking this.


00:44:26.512 --> 00:44:29.743
Only her eyes were piercing out
through this veil, but her voice...


00:44:29.915 --> 00:44:31.974
How hot was the girl
on a scale of one to 10?


00:44:32.151 --> 00:44:34.085
- An 11.
- The hotness scale only goes 10.


00:44:34.253 --> 00:44:35.948
Yeah, this girl has love potential.


00:44:36.122 --> 00:44:38.420
- Ooh, love.
- Shut it.


00:44:39.792 --> 00:44:43.922
We are gonna do this for hours
until we get it right. Even if it takes hours.


00:44:44.897 --> 00:44:48.492
Now, sing like your life depends on it.
Because, sugar, it does.


00:44:49.568 --> 00:44:51.195
We're recording.


00:44:51.504 --> 00:44:53.335
<i>Plug in the mike</i>


00:44:53.506 --> 00:44:54.734
<i>Open the curtain</i>


00:44:55.341 --> 00:44:57.275
<i>Turn on the lights</i>


00:44:57.443 --> 00:44:59.172
<i>I'm through rehearsing</i>


00:44:59.345 --> 00:45:01.677
- Dang, she's good, man.
- Told you, man.


00:45:01.847 --> 00:45:03.075
Check this out, all right?


00:45:03.249 --> 00:45:06.844
Thirty-nine girls in the singing program
which means 85 percent...


00:45:07.019 --> 00:45:08.850
...have music during the sixth period.


00:45:09.021 --> 00:45:10.852
So your girl's in one of those rooms.


00:45:11.056 --> 00:45:13.081
<i>The feeling ignites</i>


00:45:13.259 --> 00:45:14.419
<i>I'm in control</i>


00:45:14.593 --> 00:45:16.561
Oh, cut. Cut.


00:45:16.729 --> 00:45:18.594
That was subpar at best.


00:45:18.764 --> 00:45:21.289
From the top, pretty please.


00:45:22.034 --> 00:45:25.333
<i>Amazing grace</i>


00:45:25.504 --> 00:45:27.062
It's cool, I got this.


00:45:27.239 --> 00:45:29.605
Ladies, all my single ladies.


00:45:29.775 --> 00:45:32.801
My boy Luke here has a special favor
to ask of you, all right?


00:45:32.978 --> 00:45:36.072
He needs vocals
for this big show coming up, so...


00:45:36.248 --> 00:45:37.806
- My name is...
- Luke Morgan.


00:45:38.250 --> 00:45:41.117
You will put me in the Showcase.
Oh, yes, you will.


00:45:41.654 --> 00:45:45.215
- Maybe I could ask you to sing first?
- I am so gonna rock your world.


00:45:45.491 --> 00:45:48.824
<i>I love the way you love me, Luke</i>


00:45:48.994 --> 00:45:51.588
<i>Inside my head every night</i>


00:45:51.764 --> 00:45:54.232
<i>You come and kiss me good night</i>


00:45:54.400 --> 00:45:57.494
<i>Whatever you see is what you get</i>


00:45:57.670 --> 00:46:00.195
Why don't you not suck
and do it again, okay?


00:46:01.941 --> 00:46:06.537
<i>I wanna be with you forever...</i>


00:46:06.712 --> 00:46:09.681
What is going on in here? Disgusting.


00:46:09.849 --> 00:46:12.682
You two boys are not in my class.
Stop. Wait.


00:46:18.724 --> 00:46:21.921
Stop. Wait. Stop.


00:46:41.046 --> 00:46:43.344
<i>I got nothing to lose</i>


00:46:43.515 --> 00:46:44.709
<i>I've been exposed</i>


00:46:44.884 --> 00:46:47.182
<i>I'm paying my dues</i>


00:46:47.353 --> 00:46:48.718
<i>Playing the role</i>


00:46:49.555 --> 00:46:51.682
- Oh, really?
- We are back where we started.


00:46:51.857 --> 00:46:52.983
This is not good.


00:46:54.560 --> 00:46:56.357
That's her. That's her voice.


00:46:56.528 --> 00:46:58.359
Don't think you can get away from me.


00:46:58.530 --> 00:47:00.930
- Step aside. Step aside.
- Please. Wait.


00:47:01.100 --> 00:47:04.536
Okay. But first, why don't you
just both audition for me.


00:47:04.703 --> 00:47:05.727
Listen...


00:47:05.905 --> 00:47:09.341
<i>Luke, you are the one for me, yes you are</i>


00:47:09.508 --> 00:47:11.169
<i>You just don't know it yet</i>


00:47:23.022 --> 00:47:27.015
<i>Make you believe in me</i>


00:47:27.192 --> 00:47:30.184
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:30.362 --> 00:47:33.991
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:34.166 --> 00:47:38.102
<i>That I can be
Anything, anything, anything</i>


00:47:38.270 --> 00:47:42.070
<i>I'll make you believe in me</i>


00:47:42.608 --> 00:47:45.509
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:45.678 --> 00:47:48.738
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:50.549 --> 00:47:52.483
It was you?


00:47:53.152 --> 00:47:56.246
- Oh, sorry to interrupt.
- Oh, no, honey. Interrupt away.


00:47:57.189 --> 00:48:01.023
I didn't think I'd see you. It was killing me.
Because I felt like we connected.


00:48:02.661 --> 00:48:05.687
Excuse me.
Uh, how exactly did you two connect?


00:48:05.864 --> 00:48:08.628
Yeah, how did we? I mean, we did.


00:48:08.801 --> 00:48:10.928
- Through...
- With your lyrics. They just...


00:48:11.570 --> 00:48:14.300
- I can't get them out of my head.
- My lyrics. Yeah.


00:48:14.573 --> 00:48:16.336
Well, how wonderful.


00:48:16.508 --> 00:48:19.875
But, uh, Bev has to prepare
for her Showcase audition.


00:48:20.045 --> 00:48:22.309
Oh, no. She doesn't need to audition.
You're in.


00:48:23.816 --> 00:48:25.613
Do you wanna grab a bite later?


00:48:25.784 --> 00:48:26.876
- Yeah.
Wait.


00:48:27.820 --> 00:48:29.287
You have a date with detention.


00:48:29.455 --> 00:48:30.922
Actually, he has a date with me.


00:48:31.090 --> 00:48:32.819
Dear me, did I not fire you?


00:48:32.992 --> 00:48:35.688
- I have tenure.
- One call and you're wearing a paper hat...


00:48:35.861 --> 00:48:38.989
...that says "Welcome to McDonald's.
How may I take your order?"


00:48:39.164 --> 00:48:40.654
- Five calls.
- Two calls and text.


00:48:40.833 --> 00:48:42.733
Two calls, a text, several long e-mails.


00:48:42.901 --> 00:48:45.699
One text and a Tweet.
- One text and a re-Tweet.


00:48:45.871 --> 00:48:48.237
Oh, for God's sakes,
go lick a chalkboard.


00:48:48.407 --> 00:48:49.874
Fine.


00:48:50.676 --> 00:48:52.200
I hate you.


00:48:55.848 --> 00:48:59.978
Okay. Um, I'd love to write a song with you.
Let's talk about it tonight?


00:49:00.252 --> 00:49:02.186
- I'd love to.
- Okay, you're on.


00:49:08.761 --> 00:49:10.388
I've always wanted to write a song.


00:49:10.562 --> 00:49:13.759
Maybe I'll write about my skin.
They say love tightens your pores.


00:49:13.932 --> 00:49:15.399
What rhymes with pores?


00:49:15.567 --> 00:49:18.365
Chores. Bores. Sores.


